# Project Overview

This website is a MERN stack notes application that demonstrates how to build a full-stack web app from scratch. It covers the core techniques used in modern web development, from frontend design to backend APIs and database integration.

## Techniques Covered

### Frontend Techniques
- React functional components and hooks
- State management with useState and useEffect
- React Router for page navigation
- Axios for communicating with the backend
- Tailwind CSS and DaisyUI for modern UI styling
- Toast notifications for user feedback
- Loading, empty-state, and error-state handling

### Backend Techniques
- Node.js and Express server setup
- RESTful API structure
- CRUD operations for notes
- MongoDB database connection using Mongoose
- Environment variables for configuration
- CORS setup for frontend-backend communication
- Rate limiting using Upstash Redis

### Full-Stack Development Techniques
- Connecting a React frontend to an Express backend
- Sending and receiving JSON data between client and server
- Building reusable components and modular project folders
- Handling forms and user actions efficiently
- Structuring a project for scalable development

## What This Project Teaches
- How to create a complete notes app using the MERN stack
- How to build an API and connect it to a database
- How to design a responsive UI with Tailwind CSS
- How to manage client-server communication in a real project
- How to apply common web development best practices
